# Labs Structured Reference

This file reorganizes lab knowledge into the same keyed mechanic format used by other deterministic knowledge sources.
The original raw source remains preserved in public/knowledge/labs for side-by-side comparison.

Mechanic: Labs
Type: System
Domain: Research
Section: Labs
Category: Progression
Aliases: none.
Definition: Labs are research upgrades that improve scaling, caps, or specialized mechanics over time.
Behavior:
Labs are researched over time instead of purchased instantly.
Most labs are unlocked in Milestones before they can be researched.
The labs page includes research management features and quality-of-life tools.

Mechanic: Lab Switching
Type: Research Rule
Domain: Labs
Section: Labs
Category: Research Management
Aliases: switching labs
Definition: Lab Switching lets a player swap the active research to another lab.
Behavior:
When a lab is switched away from, spent coins are refunded.
Research progress is preserved and shown as green lab time.
When that lab is resumed later, the coins must be paid again.

Mechanic: Auto Research
Type: Automation Rule
Domain: Labs
Section: Labs
Category: Research Management
Aliases: auto lab; auto-research
Definition: Auto Research automatically starts the next level of the current lab after the active level completes.
Behavior:
Auto Research is toggled from the small clock or timer icon to the left of the progress bar.
Auto Research only queues the next level of the same current lab.

Mechanic: Lab Search
Type: Quality of Life
Domain: Labs
Section: Labs
Category: Navigation
Aliases: search labs
Definition: Lab Search filters labs by name so the player can find related labs without scrolling.
Behavior:
Lab Search is used when selecting a new lab.
Typing a lab name in the search bar narrows the visible lab list.

Mechanic: Lab History
Type: Quality of Life
Domain: Labs
Section: Labs
Category: Tracking
Aliases: research history
Definition: Lab History shows a chronological list of completed labs and their completion timestamps.
Behavior:
Lab History is accessed from the History tab while selecting a new lab.
The list shows labs in completion order together with the date and time each was completed.

Mechanic: Lab Slots
Type: Capacity
Domain: Gems
Section: Labs
Category: Research Capacity
Aliases: number of labs; lab count
Definition: Lab Slots determine how many labs can be researched in parallel.
Behavior:
The first lab slot unlocks in Milestones at Tier 1 Wave 30.
Players start with one slot and can unlock up to five total lab slots.
The total Gem cost to reach five slots is 4,900 Gems.

Mechanic: Lab Slot Costs
Type: Cost Ladder
Domain: Gems
Section: Labs
Category: Research Capacity
Aliases: lab slot costs
Definition: Lab Slot Costs are the Gem costs for each lab slot unlock.
Costs:
Lab slot 1 is free.
Lab slot 2 costs 100 Gems.
Lab slot 3 costs 400 Gems.
Lab slot 4 costs 1,400 Gems.
Lab slot 5 costs 3,000 Gems.

Mechanic: Lab Rushing
Type: Time Skip
Domain: Gems
Section: Labs
Category: Time Acceleration
Aliases: rushing labs; lab rush
Definition: Lab Rushing skips the entire remaining lab time by spending Gems.
Behavior:
Lab Rushing only skips the full remaining time and does not partially rush a lab.
Longer lab times have built-in discounts, so Gem cost per unit time becomes cheaper on long researches.
Gold boxing labs increases Gem rush efficiency, making rushing require fewer Gems.

Mechanic: Lab Boosting
Type: Time Acceleration
Domain: Elite Cells
Section: Labs
Category: Time Acceleration
Aliases: lab boosts; speed up labs
Definition: Lab Boosting spends Elite Cells to temporarily accelerate research speed on active labs.
Behavior:
Labs can be boosted to 1.5x, 2x, 3x, 4x, 5x, 6x, 7x, or 8x.
Boost durations are 1 hour, 8 hours, or 24 hours.
The player selects Speed Up, then a duration, then a multiplier, and the game shows the Elite Cell cost.
Lab boosts use flat-rate costs by multiplier and duration since v25.5.
Higher multipliers cost disproportionately more than the extra speed they provide, so spreading boosts across several labs is often more efficient than boosting one lab harder.
Lab boosts can be configured to auto-queue when completed.
Lab boosts only tick while a lab is slotted for research.

